Message-ID: <594a8f1774dd6838fbbc7c5ba19c8e60b212bbff.1792587545.git.mjg@fedoraproject.org>
From: Sebastian Rasmussen <sebras@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 13:16:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Bug 709768: Clear list pointer to avoid double free.

The bug shows up when signing a crafted PDF-file where a signature
object has two reference dictionaries that specify which field
objects should be included in the digest: one references a
specific field, and the other one specifies /All implying that
all fields should be included.

When encountering /All MuPDF drops the list of field names that
created when parsing the first signature reference dictionary.
While doing so, all names in that list are freed, as is the list
itself, but crucially the pointer to the list is not reset to
NULL.

Later on when the code for freeing the list is called again,
MuPDF attempts to free the stale list pointer.

As mentioned in the report by Suyuan Wang the fix is to set the
list pointer to NULL when the list of field names is freed.
---
 source/pdf/pdf-xref.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/source/pdf/pdf-xref.c b/source/pdf/pdf-xref.c
index ca25fea42..db21647ee 100644
--- a/source/pdf/pdf-xref.c
+++ b/source/pdf/pdf-xref.c
@@ -4176,6 +4176,7 @@ free_char_list(fz_context *ctx, char_list *c)
 	for (i = c->len-1; i >= 0; i--)
 		fz_free(ctx, c->list[i]);
 	fz_free(ctx, c->list);
+	c->list = NULL;
 	c->len = 0;
 	c->max = 0;
 }
